# Settings portal colour-scheme (CS-1057 / TRK-1211, 2026-08-22). The gtk
# portal serves org.freedesktop.impl.portal.Settings — the only way a Flatpak
# or Electron app learns the OS is dark — by READING GSettings
# org.gnome.desktop.interface color-scheme. Both were only transitive here
# (dconf via gtk4, the schemas via xdg-desktop-portal-gtk), so a package
# shuffle could silently drop them and leave `gsettings set` writing to the
# memory backend, i.e. nowhere. Pinned on purpose; nyxus-session-start writes
# the keys at login.
# dconf                    : the GSettings backend that actually persists
# gsettings-desktop-schemas: org.gnome.desktop.interface (color-scheme, gtk-theme, …)
