# hicolor-icon-theme was NEVER declared here — it only existed on the image
# as a transitive accident of other packages pulling files into
# usr/share/icons/hicolor/, with six size dirs and no index.theme at all.
# hicolor is the freedesktop.org FALLBACK theme: every icon lookup that
# misses in the active theme (Papirus, or whatever the user picks) falls
# through to hicolor last, and every one of this build's own nyxus-*.svg/png
# app icons is shipped INTO hicolor's own directories rather than a named
# theme of its own. Declaring the package (not hand-writing index.theme in
# this tree — that path is package-owned and not in hicolor-icon-theme's
# backup=(), so a profile-tree copy aborts the pacstrap transaction the same
# way the blueman-manager.desktop conflict did, per gate 13q8) is what turns
# "icons happen to land in a directory with this name" into "a real,
# resolvable icon theme with a valid index.theme", which pacstrap installs.
# Gate 13vp checks this by content coverage, not by the package's name alone.
hicolor-icon-theme
# ── vte4 IS THE ONE NYXUS Terminal NEEDS (WIP-319, 2026-08-11) ────
# `vte3` ships the GTK3 binding and installs Vte-2.91.typelib. NYXUS
# Terminal is a GTK4 app and asks for `Vte 3.91`, which comes only
# from `vte4`. Without it the require_version() raises on every
# launch, the except branch draws the label "VTE not available", and
# the build's own terminal opens a window that cannot run a single
# command — proven by launching it on the booted 2026-08-11 ISO.
#
# Keep BOTH: vte3 is a dependency of other packaged GTK3 software,
# and removing it is a separate question from adding this one.
#
# Super+Return and the Start tile exec ghostty. Other emulators are not
# shipped. vte4 stays for any GTK VTE leftover, not as a second Terminal.
vte4
vte3
vte-common
# ── gtksourceview5 — NYXUS Notes is an editor now (WIP-331, 2026-08-11) ──
# Notes was one textarea. The owner asked for a Notepad++-class editor, so
# it gained tabs, line numbers, syntax highlighting, find/replace and
# go-to-line, all of which are GtkSourceView.
#
# This line exists because of vte4 directly above it. That entry is the
# record of what happens when an app asks gi for a typelib the image does
# not carry: require_version raises, an except branch draws an apology, and
# the app ships dead through green gates. Notes degrades to a plain
# Gtk.TextView if GtkSource is missing rather than dying — but it should
# never have to, so the package is named here in the same commit as the code
# that needs it.
gtksourceview5
python
python-gobject
python-pip
python-cairo
python-psutil
python-cryptography

# ── NYXUS Studio's deps, packaged so first login does NOT pip (WIP-322) ──
# nyxus-studio.tgz's install.sh runs, at FIRST LOGIN:
#     pip install --user sounddevice soundfile scipy trimesh
# for any of the four it cannot already import. On a live stick that is a
# download from PyPI before the user has done anything — the same fault as
# SAGE's chromadb, and it slipped past audit.sh 15 for the same reason: the
# pip lives inside a cache payload, not in an app file.
#
# The installer checks `python3 -c "import <pkg>"` FIRST and skips the pip
# when the import succeeds, so packaging these makes that branch dead code
# rather than needing the tarball repacked.
#
# ⚠ `sounddevice` is deliberately NOT here: it has no official Arch package
# (AUR only), and this profile has no AUR path — local-repo carries only the
# owner's Kage-Ryu kernel. It is therefore the one first-login pip that can
# still fire, and gate 13ui names it rather than pretending otherwise.
python-soundfile
python-scipy
python-trimesh
python-requests
python-pillow
python-dnspython

