whois

# ── input methods (WIP-118) ───────────────────────────────────────
# The build shipped noto-fonts-cjk, so Chinese, Japanese and Korean RENDERED
# perfectly — and there was no way to TYPE a single character of any of them.
# That asymmetry is worse than shipping neither: the system looks like it
# supports those languages right up until someone tries to use it. Against a
# brief of "an everyday system anyone can use", "anyone" meant "anyone who
# writes in a Latin script".
#
# fcitx5 over ibus because fcitx5's Wayland frontend speaks text-input-v3,
# which is what wlroots implements; ibus still leans on the X11 path.
fcitx5
fcitx5-configtool
fcitx5-gtk
fcitx5-qt
# Engines. Chinese (pinyin/shuangpin + more), Korean (hangul), Japanese
# (anthy), and the table engines that cover a long tail of other scripts.
fcitx5-chinese-addons
fcitx5-hangul
fcitx5-anthy
fcitx5-table-extra

