# WIP-121 was a FALSE GAP, and the way it was wrong is worth keeping.
#
# The audit searched packages.x86_64 for `libva-mesa-driver`, did not find it,
# and concluded AMD machines had no hardware video decode. The package name was
# the wrong test: Arch folded that package INTO mesa, which now carries
# `provides: libva-mesa-driver` and `replaces: libva-mesa-driver<1:24.2.7-1`.
# mesa has been in this list all along, so AMD VAAPI already worked.
#
# Adding the name would have been worse than useless — it is not in the repos
# at all any more, so pacstrap would have failed and taken the whole bake with
# it. `mesa-vdpau` is gone the same way. Caught by querying the Arch package
# database before trusting the audit's own finding.
#
# The lesson, which is the same one as WIP-117: "is the name present?" is not
# the same question as "does the capability exist?"
vulkan-intel
lib32-vulkan-intel
vulkan-icd-loader
lib32-vulkan-icd-loader
vulkan-tools
intel-gpu-tools
mesa
lib32-mesa
mesa-utils

# ── GPU drivers — AMD (TRK-1205 / CS-1058, 2026-08-22) ──────────────
# AMD is a TARGET now, not an accident. The owner's 2026-08-20 ruling: the OS
# must pick up "any typical PC ~2012-now" — and his own second machine (the
# Alienware 15, Ryzen 7 260) carries an AMD iGPU. Until today Vulkan on any
# AMD box resolved to nothing: the 2026-07-14 note further down dropped
# vulkan-radeon as "hardware-locked build for the MSI GS77", which this block
# supersedes. What AMD needed and now has:
#   vulkan-radeon / lib32-       : RADV, the Mesa Vulkan driver for GCN 1.2+
#                                  (Radeon HD 7000 era onward, 2012 = the
#                                  ruling's own cut line)
#   switcheroo-control           : D-Bus dual-GPU reporter for hybrid boxes
#                                  (AMD iGPU + NVIDIA dGPU = the Alienware);
#                                  180 KiB, dbus-activated
# Already here all along, for the record: mesa (radeonsi GL **and**
# `provides: libva-mesa-driver`, i.e. AMD VA-API — see the WIP-121 note
# above), lib32-mesa, linux-firmware (the amdgpu/ firmware set), amd-ucode.
# The support matrix itself lives in ONE place — airootfs
# /usr/local/bin/nyxus-gpu-probe (`--matrix`) — and gate 13s50 derives this
# block's package names from it rather than restating them.
vulkan-radeon
lib32-vulkan-radeon
switcheroo-control

