# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# DE COMPLETENESS — WAVE 1 (rev 2026-08-01)
# docs/DE_COMPLETENESS_AND_EDITIONS_2026-07-31.md §2.1
# Every entry here backs something that was already built, shipped and
# exposed in Settings but could not run for want of a package.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# gtk4-layer-shell — the GTK4 layer-shell binding.
# /opt/nyxus/desktop/nyxus_desktop.py is a complete GTK4 layer-shell desktop
# client (wallpaper paint per-monitor at the BOTTOM layer + right-click →
# nyxus-context-menu.sh). It does gi.require_version("Gtk4LayerShell","1.0")
# and this profile only ever listed `gtk-layer-shell`, which is the GTK **3**
# library and a different package. The import guard's fallback is
# os.execvp("swaybg", …) with a message on stderr nobody reads, so the desktop
# layer degraded to a plain wallpaper with no right-click and NO visible error.
gtk4-layer-shell

# loupe — image viewer. There was no image viewer on the ISO at all, so every
# PNG/JPEG resolved to Firefox (which claims those types) and opened in a
# browser tab. Needed before a mimeapps.list has anything to point at.

# poppler — the PDF engine behind Nyxus Reader (nyxus_reader.py renders with
# pdftocairo / pdfinfo / pdftotext / pdftohtml, "needs exactly one package —
# poppler"). zathura + zathura-pdf-mupdf REMOVED 2026-08-22 (TRK-1252 /
# CS-1153): Reader is the PDF viewer and mimeapps.list's application/pdf
# points at nyxus-reader.desktop first; the zathura fallback id is gone with
# the package (13pk would otherwise name a handler nothing provides). Store
# shelf: Search (`zathura`).
poppler

# qt5ct + qt6ct — Qt theming, and the ONE consistent option available.
# skel already ships ~/.config/qt5ct/qt5ct.conf and ~/.config/qt6ct/qt6ct.conf
# (style=Fusion + the custom nyxus-galaxy palette) and NEITHER
# package was installed, so nothing read either file and every Qt app rendered
# default light grey.
#
# The DE study's §2.1 item 3 asked for `adwaita-qt5` + `adwaita-qt6` instead
# (to match QT_QPA_PLATFORMTHEME=adwaita-dark in /etc/environment.d). Those
# packages NO LONGER EXIST in the Arch repos — `pacman -Si adwaita-qt5` and
# `adwaita-qt6` both resolve to nothing on a fully synced box (upstream
# adwaita-qt is archived), and pacstrap ABORTS on an unknown package, so
# listing them would have failed the bake outright. qt5ct/qt6ct is the
# alternative the study itself offers in §1.3 row 7, and it is the better one
# because the config it needs is already in skel and already on palette.
qt5ct
qt6ct
# ── Kvantum (WIP-343) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# A Qt STYLE, not a platform theme, so one config applies across Qt5
# AND Qt6 — which is why the owner's theme brief names it. It is the
# only way to give both toolkit generations identical button shapes
# and toggle mechanics; QT_QPA_PLATFORMTHEME can only ever name one
# plugin, and naming qt6ct (see environment.d/90-nyxus-theme.conf)
# leaves Qt5 apps falling back. Packaged now so the theme itself is
# unblocked; writing it is still owed.
kvantum

# ffmpegthumbnailer — video thumbnails in Files. Image thumbnails already work
# (nautilus pulls glycin); video and PDF had none. `tumbler` is deliberately
# NOT added — it serves the thunar family, and no thunar-family file manager
# ships here.
ffmpegthumbnailer

# ── DE completeness Wave 2 · the MIME substrate (§2.2) ────────────────────
# Both of these were ALREADY on the ISO, and both only by accident. Listing
# them explicitly is the whole point: the accidents are load-bearing and one of
# them breaks the moment a lighter edition drops a browser.
#
# xdg-utils — xdg-open and xdg-mime themselves, i.e. the mechanism the entire
# mimeapps.list depends on. It reached the image only because CHROMIUM
# hard-depends on it — an implicit dependency is not a listing, and the day
# chromium moves or is dropped, xdg-open and xdg-mime would leave with it and
# nothing would open anything by association. So it is listed OUTRIGHT here.
# (TRK-3681: this note used to cite packages.x86_64.lean, which already
# dropped chromium, as the live proof. That list is deleted — one product,
# one package list — so the reason is stated directly instead.)
xdg-utils
# xdg-user-dirs — ~/Documents, ~/Downloads, ~/Pictures and friends.
# xdg-user-dirs-gtk was a nautilus hard-dep; listed here so dropping
# GNOME Files does not lose GTK bookmarks / first-login dir update.
xdg-user-dirs
xdg-user-dirs-gtk

# ── NYXUS Store: the software catalogue ───────────────────────────
# This is what makes the Store a store rather than a package manager with
# buttons. It ships the standard AppStream metadata for every application
# in the repositories into /usr/share/swcatalog/ — the same data GNOME
# Software reads — and `nyxus_appstream.py` parses it with the standard
# library, so NOTHING here depends on the `appstream` package or its GIR
# bindings.
#
# Measured against the 20260606 drop, 2026-08-12:
#   1179 applications with real names, summaries and full descriptions
#    828 with screenshots (remote URLs, fetched and cached on demand)
#   1179 with an icon ON LOCAL DISK
#
# That last line is why the Store works offline. Only screenshots need a
# network; everything else, including every icon, is read from this
# package. 22.50 MiB installed.
archlinux-appstream-data

# ── archiso runtime requirements ──────────────────────────────────
arch-install-scripts
archinstall
archiso
squashfs-tools
pacman-contrib
reflector
rsync
which
