# TRK-3658 · timeshift comes from [extra], NOT from the AUR.
# It was an `_aur_build timeshift` and it FAILED on the 2026-09-01 bake:
#     error: target not found: libsoup
# The AUR recipe still names libsoup, which Arch replaced with libsoup3, so
# that build cannot resolve its own dependency and the package never landed.
# The ISO therefore shipped Backup with nothing behind it — the app opens,
# checks HAS_TIMESHIFT, finds nothing and degrades to a page that cannot take
# a snapshot. verify-app-launch could not see it because degrading gracefully
# is exactly what the app is written to do.
# `extra/timeshift` is current (25.12.4-1) and needs no build at all.
timeshift
# TRK-3658 · ananicy-cpp comes from [extra] too, for the same reason.
# `_aur_build ananicy-cpp` FAILED on the 2026-09-01 bake and it was not a
# dependency problem - the AUR source does not COMPILE against current GCC:
#     error: 'memset' is not a member of 'std'
#     error: 'getpid' was not declared in this scope
# which is the transitive-include tightening recent GCC shipped. The packaged
# build (extra/ananicy-cpp 1.2.0-1) is current and needs no compiler of ours.
# customize_airootfs.sh still enables ananicy-cpp.service; only the BUILD moves.
ananicy-cpp
